From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:43:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: keep the link when the supplicant closes the
 port

Roams now reassociate on the second access point, but the supplicant drops
the handshake's first message with "No SSID info found" and the access
point gives up after four tries. The supplicant had lost its network.

Reading the log and code: it closes the port as it starts a roam, which
reaches the driver as AUTHORIZED to ASSOC. The driver took any downward step
as the end of the link and reported a connection loss, so the supplicant
saw a disconnect mid-roam.

Only stop the data on that step. mac80211's own disconnect for the new
authentication then takes the link down as for any driver.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index 8b7fb99dc..38f8a8875 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -1733,6 +1733,25 @@ static int mt6797_mac_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 				enum ieee80211_sta_state old,
 				enum ieee80211_sta_state new)
 {
+	/* The supplicant closes the port as it starts a roam, while the link stays
+	 * up. Ending the link here reports a connection loss, and the supplicant
+	 * then forgets its network with the roam under way. Only stop the data.
+	 */
+	if (old == IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED && new == IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC) {
+		struct mt6797_mac *mac = hw->priv;
+		unsigned long flags;
+
+		mutex_lock(&mac->mutex);
+		if (vif == mac->vif) {
+			mac->ccmp_rx.authorized = false;
+			mac->ccmp_gtk_rx.authorized = false;
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&mac->join_queue.lock, flags);
+			mac->ccmp_tx_ready = false;
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mac->join_queue.lock, flags);
+		}
+		mutex_unlock(&mac->mutex);
+		return 0;
+	}
 	/* mac80211 station teardown must not fail; no peer command is
 	 * admitted by this incomplete upward-transition implementation.
 	 */
-- 
